      "schema_version": "aspr_gear",
      "text": "This study proposes that weak CD47–SIRPα signaling permits incomplete macrophage digestion of prostate cancer cells, generating tumor hybrid cells with elevated c-Myc and mixed macrophage-like programs. It combines co-culture, perturbation, xenograft, spatial/single-cell, and patient-tissue analyses to relate THCs to metastatic prostate cancer features, while leaving their origin, immune function, and clinical predictive value incompletely resolved."
    },
